+# CONTRACT — Factory Reset
+
+## Part 1: `solveToggle(machine: Machine): number[] | null`
+
+Model: GF(2) linear system. Each button is a vector over N lights; pressing a
+subset = XOR of vectors must equal target. Find min-size subset, tie-break
+lexicographically smallest sorted index array; null if unsatisfiable.
+
+Behaviors:
+- [ ] Returns sorted-ascending array of button indices → test: output is sorted.
+- [ ] Empty target (all false) → returns `[]` (press nothing). → test.
+- [ ] Unsatisfiable system → returns `null`. → test: the TASK.md example returns null.
+- [ ] Finds a valid solution: pressing returned buttons yields target. → test: simulate.
+- [ ] Returns MINIMUM number of buttons. → test: cross-check vs brute force.
+- [ ] Ties broken by lexicographically smallest index set. → test: crafted + brute force.
+- [ ] Toggle order irrelevant / duplicate light indices in one button cancel. → test.
+- [ ] Handles M=40, N=40 in <5s (rank-deficient incl. all-buttons-same-light). → perf test.
+- [ ] M=0 with all-false target → `[]`; with any true → `null`. → test.
+- [ ] Random cross-check (many small instances) matches brute force exactly. → test.
+
+Verify: `npm test`, `npm run build`, `npm run lint`.
+
+## Part 2: `solveCounter(lights, buttons, modulus): number[] | null`
+
+Model: GF(p) linear system (p prime). result[i] = presses of button i in [0,p).
+A·x ≡ lights (mod p). Minimize total presses (integer sum), tie-break
+lexicographically smallest result array; null if unsatisfiable.
+
+Behaviors:
+- [ ] Returns array length M, each entry in [0, modulus). → test.
+- [ ] Valid solution: applying presses mod p yields target counters. → test: simulate.
+- [ ] MINIMUM total presses (sum). → test: cross-check vs brute force.
+- [ ] Ties broken by lexicographically smallest result array. → test: brute force.
+- [ ] Unsatisfiable → `null`. → test.
+- [ ] All-zero target → all-zero result `[0,...]`. → test.
+- [ ] mod 2 reduces to toggle-like behavior (cross-check). → test.
+- [ ] Duplicate counter indices in one button increment multiple times. → test.
+- [ ] Handles large free dimension via small-rank path (M>N, e.g. 40 buttons 1 counter). → test.
+- [ ] Handles up to 40 buttons / 40 counters / mod 97 in <5s. → perf test.
+- [ ] Random cross-check (small instances) matches brute force exactly. → test.
+
+Done = every box checked, tests pass, build clean, lint clean, self-review clean.
